{"name":"Pink Lady","hex":"#f3d7b6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Pink Lady","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A Cripps Pink apple.","A gin-based cocktail with grenadine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Pink_Lady"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Pink Lady (musical)","blocks":[{"text":"The Pink Lady is an Edwardian musical comedy composed by Ivan Caryll, which ran for a very successful 312 performances on Broadway in 1911 before becoming an ongoing favorite of regional producers in the Midwest. The story and lyrics by C.M.S. McLellan, about an antiques dealer, were adapted from a French farce, The Satyr, by Georges Berr and Marcel Guiltemand"}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/The_Pink_Lady_by_Hamilton_King_-_1911.jpg/330px-The_Pink_Lady_by_Hamilton_King_-_1911.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Pink_Lady_(musical)","wikidata":"Q16985531"},{"title":"Pink Lady (art)","blocks":[{"text":"The Pink Lady was a painting on a rock face near Malibu, California in 1966. The painting was created by Lynne Seemayer (1936–2017), an artist and paralegal from Northridge, California. It was a 60-foot tall depiction of a frolicking nude woman."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b5/Pink-lady.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink_Lady_(art)","wikidata":"Q7196036"},{"title":"Pink Lady (duo)","blocks":[{"text":"Pink Lady  is a Japanese female pop music duo of the late 1970s and early 1980s, featuring Mie and Keiko Masuda. In Japan, they are remembered for a run of pop-chart hits from roughly 1976 to 1979, but in the United States, they are best known for their short-lived 1980 NBC TV variety show Pink Lady and Jeff."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Pink_Lady%2C_1979_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Pink_Lady%2C_1979_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink_Lady_(duo)","wikidata":"Q498416"},{"title":"Lady","blocks":[{"text":"A lady is a woman who behaves in a polite way. Once used to describe only women of a high social class or status, the female counterpart of lord, now it may refer to any adult woman, as gentleman can be used for men."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lady","wikidata":"Q1378024"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Pinklady1.jpg/330px-Pinklady1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Pinklady1.jpg/330px-Pinklady1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Programme for The Pink Lady","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APinklady1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Pink_Lady_1980.jpg/500px-Pink_Lady_1980.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Pink_Lady_1980.jpg/500px-Pink_Lady_1980.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pink Lady in 1980","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APink_Lady_1980.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Pink_Lady_and_Jeff_1980.jpg/500px-Pink_Lady_and_Jeff_1980.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Pink_Lady_and_Jeff_1980.jpg/500px-Pink_Lady_and_Jeff_1980.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pink Lady and Jeff Altman in a promotional picture of their eponymous show, 1980","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APink_Lady_and_Jeff_1980.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://